// Every module in this repository, wired together for local development.
//
// The provider modules (stripe, paypal, razorpay) each `require` a published
// version of the root module. Without this workspace they would compile against
// that published version even here, so a breaking change to the root would pass
// CI while silently breaking every provider. The workspace overrides that
// requirement with the working tree.
//
// This file is committed on purpose. It used to be gitignored, which meant it
// worked on a developer's machine but not in CI: GitHub Actions cloned a tree
// without it and tested every provider against the last published root.
//
// No module in this repo carries a `replace` directive; this file is the only
// place local resolution is configured, and it is ignored entirely when someone
// depends on any of these modules.
//
// Releasing bumps each provider's `require` to the new root tag (see
// CONTRIBUTING.md). That stays on main safely, precisely because the workspace
// still points local builds at the working tree.
//
// To reproduce a consumer's build instead, set GOWORK=off.

go 1.24

use (
	.
	./paypal
	./razorpay
	./stripe
)
